            <ArticleTitle>Iliopsoas bursitis-an unusual presentation of metastatic bone disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>285-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diagnostic uncertainty concerning the nature of an enlarging inguinal mass in an elderly male with a short history of hip pain was resolved by a combination of ultrasound and magnetic resonance imaging (MRI). Subsequent investigations showed that the enlarged iliopsoas bursa, which contained a number of atypical cells, was an unusual presenting feature of a destructive metastatic lesion in the right hip.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
